      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T16:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The export list is R7RS appendix A\u0027s, which leaves out `syntax-rules` and the auxiliary syntax: `else`, `\u003d\u003e`, `unquote`, `unquote-splicing`, `...` and `_`. R5RS defines all of them, and without them a program that imports only this library breaks. With the CLI built from this change:\n\n```\n(import (scheme r5rs)) (display (cond (#f 1) (else 2)))\n  → else is not bound: is it imported?\n(import (scheme r5rs)) (display (case 3 ((1) \u0027a) (else \u0027b)))\n  → case: no pattern matches this use\n(import (scheme r5rs)) (display (cond ((assv 2 \u0027((2 . x))) \u003d\u003e cdr) (else \u0027none)))\n  → \u003d\u003e is not bound: is it imported?\n(import (scheme r5rs)) (define-syntax swap! (syntax-rules () ...))\n  → syntax-rules is not bound: is it imported?\n(import (scheme r5rs)) (display `(1 ,(+ 1 1) ,@(list 3)))\n  → (1 (unquote (+ 1 1)) (unquote-splicing (list 3)))\n```\n\nThe last one is the worst: no error, just the wrong value. `scheme-report-environment` already adds exactly these names. Exporting them from the library too would make `(import (scheme r5rs))` usable on its own, and a test along the lines of the five above would keep it that way.",
      "revId": "2b66bf529376436485007409d820d94628e703c3",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
